  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion-background:pbps-rough-mean-gradient",
    "anchor": "Fixed PBPS2609.06905v1 C.1 density/closedness passage and C.2 sharp compact estimate toward B.13; actual rough-input conditional mean in the SAME canonical closed-gradient graph and sharp energy estimate. Source C2/two Hessian/positive capped eta retained.",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
    "original_text": "Attributed ASTIS-authored full-L2 closed conditional mean-gradient integration for fixed PBPS C.1/C.2 toward B.13, not separately defined weak-H1 or full Gamma norm identity.\nLet E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v, η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ and Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd and EVERY-y S_y=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)). Then ν is a probability. There is a densely defined closable real linear gradient G:L²(ν)⇀L²(ν;E), whose graph consists exactly of AE classes (φ,∇φ) for smooth compactly supported φ, and whose closure has closed graph. There are one bounded linear T:L²(ν)→L²(ν) and one bounded linear K:L²(ν)→L²(ν;E), both chosen before all arbitrary rough u∈L²(ν). For every u, (Tu,Ku)∈graph(Ḡ), ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S_y(dx) AE ν, and u,u² are integrable under S_y for AE y. With c=(1−αη)²/[4(1+αη)], η‖Ku‖²≤c(‖u‖²−‖Tu‖²) and 4η‖Ku‖²≤‖u‖²−‖Tu‖². No compactness, centering, extra moment, supplied kernel/operator/domain or convergence certificate is assumed for rough u. This is the closed compact-gradient formulation of the source density/closedness passage and sharp estimate; a separately defined weak-H1 equivalence and full Gamma/B13 identity are not claimed.\nSource boundary: Fixed PBPS2609.06905v1 C.1 density/closedness passage and C.2 sharp compact estimate toward B.13; actual rough-input conditional mean in the SAME canonical closed-gradient graph and sharp energy estimate. Source C2/two Hessian/positive capped eta retained.\nExplicit extension: Finite real Hilbert/Borel including rank0 extends printed finite Euclidean presentation. Actual closed compact-gradient graph is advertised explicitly; separately defined weak-H1 equivalence and Gamma norm identity are not claimed.\nActual objects: SAME actual mu/J/nu and EVERY-y literal source S; one dense closable genuine compact-gradient core G, one actual bounded T and one bounded K chosen BEFORE every u in full L2(nu). T is the AE source conditional mean; (T u,K u) lies in G.closure.graph; sharp coefficient c=(1-alpha*eta)^2/[4(1+alpha*eta)] and source4eta inequality.\nConsumer: Actual rough-input macroscopic coercivity step in PBPS B.13/half-turn hypocoercivity consumes the genuine conditional mean gradient and exact4eta defect. Subsequent source weak-H1 adapter/Gamma remain explicitly separate.",
    "text_sha256": "f7cec8389ed0634bcab13fa770a5d110acde3d55bcac66d4f2ec65e5baf278ed"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.RoughMeanGradient.actual_rough_mean_gradient",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/RoughMeanGradient.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α : ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E,\n      (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ (β : ℝ)*‖v‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β : ℝ)*η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n      (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n    let ν := J.snd\n    let S := fun y : E => (volume : Measure E).tilted\n      (fun x => -V ((1/2 : ℝ) • (y+x)) - ‖y-x‖^2/(8*η))\n    IsProbabilityMeasure ν ∧\n      ∃ G : Lp ℝ 2 ν →ₗ.[ℝ] Lp E 2 ν,\n        Dense (G.domain : Set (Lp ℝ 2 ν)) ∧ G.IsClosable ∧ G.closure.IsClosed ∧\n        (∀ (u : Lp ℝ 2 ν) (v : Lp E 2 ν), (u,v) ∈ G.graph ↔\n          ∃ φ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ ∞ φ ∧ HasCompactSupport φ ∧\n            u =ᵐ[ν] φ ∧ v =ᵐ[ν] gradient φ) ∧\n        ∃ T : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n          ∃ K : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp E 2 ν,\n            ∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n              (T u,K u) ∈ G.closure.graph ∧ ‖T u‖ ≤ ‖u‖ ∧\n              (T u : E → ℝ) =ᵐ[ν] (fun y => ∫ x, u x ∂S y) ∧\n              (∀ᵐ y ∂ν, Integrable (u : E → ℝ) (S y) ∧\n                Integrable (fun x => (u x)^2) (S y)) ∧\n              η*‖K u‖^2 ≤\n                (1-(α : ℝ)*η)^2/(4*(1+(α : ℝ)*η)) * (‖u‖^2-‖T u‖^2) ∧\n              4*η*‖K u‖^2 ≤ ‖u‖^2-‖T u‖^2",
    "statement_sha256": "130d1dc6206efba4b1169638714ed46f243b057f1c1586af44b5800ad53af4b7",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space with canonical volume; rank zero allowed. V is C2; positive alpha<=beta, both exact displayed global Hessian bounds, eta>0 and beta*eta<=1 are original source hypotheses.",
      "Measure.tilted denotes normalized exponential tilt. mu is exactly volume.tilted(-V); J is the actual independent pushforward of mu.prod(stdGaussian E) by (x,z)->(x,x+sqrt(eta)*z); nu=J.snd. S(y) is the exact displayed normalized reflected volume tilt at every y, not a caller measure or certificate.",
      "Lp F2nu denotes AE classes of strongly measurable square-integrable functions. Its chosen coercion is a strongly measurable representative. Finite dimension of E does not make either Lp space finite dimensional.",
      "G is an actual real partially defined linear gradient map. Its domain is dense in full real L2nu. Its graph equals precisely all pairs represented AE by one smooth compactly supported real phi and its Euclidean gradient. G.IsClosable means its topological graph closure is again single-valued; G.closure is that partial linear map and IsClosed means its graph is closed.",
      "One G, one bounded real linear T:L2nu->L2nu and one bounded real linear K:L2nu->vectorL2nu are chosen BEFORE every arbitrary rough u. (Tu,Ku) in G.closure.graph means Tu has the closed compact-gradient derivative Ku. No identification with a separately chosen weak-Sobolev convention is implicit.",
      "For every rough u, norm(Tu)<=norm(u) and Tu equals the actual S conditional integral AE nu. Both u and u squared are integrable under S(y) only AE nu. Every-y kernel law does not imply pointwise rough integral equality or pointwise C1.",
      "The displayed sharp coefficient is c=(1-alpha*eta)^2/[4(1+alpha*eta)]. The conclusions are eta*norm(Ku)^2<=c*(norm(u)^2-norm(Tu)^2) and 4eta*norm(Ku)^2<=norm(u)^2-norm(Tu)^2. Alpha*eta=1 and rank zero are allowed. No caller kernel/operator/coherence/convergence/domain certificate, centering, compactness or additional moment premise occurs.",
      "This statement makes no separately defined weak-H1 equivalence, Gamma/function calculus, algorithmic dynamics/mixing/complexity/main result or unbounded-cost conclusion."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-rough-mean-gradient56/tests.1.log PASS3899: actual joint BMu rough-difference consumer and alphaeta1 full K=0 endpoint; main+two Tests standard3."
